## The idea

Keep two positions in a sorted list and move them towards each other. If the sum is too small, move the left one right. If it is too big, move the right one left.

## When to use it

- the data is sorted (or you can sort it)
- you look for a pair or a window

```cpp
int l = 0, r = n - 1;
while (l < r) {
    int s = a[l] + a[r];
    if (s == target) break;
    if (s < target) l++; else r--;
}
```
